From 4b63d7ced75d9e907dc7a3ef2163ae593cc76014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:59:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The weekly SITREP: Monday 7 AM, facts by code, one checked
 paragraph

Each client's owner gets a SITREP on Monday at 7 AM their time for the
Monday-to-Sunday week before; Jerome gets a copy. Sent on its own, as
Jerome decided; a week with nothing to report is skipped.

- Code gathers the facts: drafts, form requests, voice notes, items that
  needed the owner, emergencies, answers taught, problems fixed, hours,
  with the week before alongside.
- Claude Sonnet 5.5 writes one short paragraph from counts and open
  questions only, never a customer's name or an email subject. Code drops
  the paragraph if any number is not on the fact sheet, or it has a
  percentage, a dollar amount or a spelled-out quantity.
- Time you got back = counts x minutes per task, standard minutes until a
  client's own are agreed; the report says which.
- POST /api/admin/sitrep previews or resends. A failed send is recorded
  and reported, and does not retry on its own.

Also: the second look gets its own daily counter, so SITREP calls can't
use it up, and the brief's cost line says Sonnet calls.

New test_sitrep.mjs (53 checks); all 10 suites and check_site.py pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
